#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283843 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4daa6bc-1c9a-5c23-8032-4d70435d9388" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Vector Given Its Image Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be4844fc-62f3-5141-b816-71872e8421ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be4844fc-62f3-5141-b816-71872e8421ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283845} :answer-field/id #uuid "87a3bcfe-7825-5a70-9588-8df57bd4628c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0674fdce-1eea-5b24-8118-caf0022c70b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0674fdce-1eea-5b24-8118-caf0022c70b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283847} :answer-field/id #uuid "f82772f8-6514-5852-b19f-dd8ff12e84c9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "daabe69c-e766-509d-b9e2-4798548ebdd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-317436" :question/problem "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$\n\n| $v=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(2)(7)-(3)(5)}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
